          <h2 is-upgraded=3D"" id=3D"create-a-firebase-project" data-text=
=3D"Create a Firebase project" tabindex=3D"-1">Create a Firebase project</h=
2>
<ol type=3D"1">
<li>Sign into the <a href=3D"https://console.firebase.google.com/" target=
=3D"_blank">Firebase console</a> using your Google Account.</li>
<li>Click the button to create a new project, and then enter a project name=
 (for example, <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">Tera Bites</code>).<br><a=
side class=3D"special"><p>This project name is used as a display name in Fi=
rebase interfaces, and Firebase auto-creates a unique project ID based on t=
his project name. Note that you can optionally click the <strong>Edit</stro=
ng> icon now to set your preferred project ID, but you cannot change this I=
D after project creation.</p>
</aside>
</li>
<li>Click <strong>Continue</strong>.</li>
<li>If prompted, review and accept the <a href=3D"https://firebase.google.c=
om/terms" target=3D"_blank">Firebase terms</a>, and then click <strong>Cont=
inue</strong>.</li>
<li><em>(Optional)</em> Enable AI assistance in the Firebase console (calle=
d "Gemini in Firebase").</li>
<li>For this codelab, you do <strong><em>not</em></strong> need Google Anal=
ytics, so <strong><em>toggle off</em></strong> the Google Analytics option.=
</li>
<li>Click <strong>Create project</strong>, wait for your project to provisi=
on, and then click <strong>Continue</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<h2 is-upgraded=3D"" id=3D"download-the-code" data-text=3D"Download the cod=
e" tabindex=3D"-1">Download the code</h2>
<p>Run the following commands to clone the sample code for this codelab:</p=
>
