<p>Open the <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">firebase-pnv-android</code> =
directory in Android Studio.</p>
<h2 is-upgraded=3D"" id=3D"connect-your-android-project-to-firebase" data-t=
ext=3D"Connect your Android project to Firebase" tabindex=3D"-1">Connect yo=
ur Android project to Firebase</h2>
<ol type=3D"1">
<li>In the Firebase console, in the center of the project overview page, cl=
ick the <strong>Android</strong> icon or <strong>Add app</strong> to launch=
 the app creation workflow.</li>
<li>In the <strong>Android package name</strong> field, enter the app's pac=
kage name: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">com.google.firebase.example.f=
pnv</code>.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Register app</strong>.</li>
<li>Follow the instructions to download the <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"l=
tr">google-services.json</code> file, and move it into the <code translate=
=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">app/</code> directory of the code you just downloaded.<=
/li>
<li>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<h2 is-upgraded=3D"" id=3D"enable-firebase-ai-logic" data-text=3D"Enable Fi=
rebase AI Logic" tabindex=3D"-1">Enable Firebase AI Logic</h2>
<p>This codelab uses Firebase AI Logic to power the AI voice agent. To enab=
le Firebase AI Logic in your Firebase project:</p>
<ol type=3D"1">
<li>In the Firebase console, go to <strong>AI Services</strong> &gt; <a hre=
f=3D"https://console.firebase.google.com/project/_/ailogic/?useAutoProject=
=3Dtrue" target=3D"_blank"><strong>AI Logic</strong></a>.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Get started</strong>.</li>
<li>Choose to use the <em>Gemini Developer API</em> by clicking <strong>Get=
 started with this API</strong>.</li>
<li>Continue with the remainder of the guided setup workflow steps.</li>
</ol>
<aside class=3D"warning"><p><strong>Warning</strong>: Firebase automaticall=
y enforces Firebase App Check for AI Logic during the guided setup workflow=
 in the Firebase console. This codelab hasn't yet been updated with the ins=
tructions to accommodate this auto-enforcement (specifically how to configu=
re the App Check <em>debug provider</em>). <strong>To continue this codelab=
</strong>, you can try to <a href=3D"https://firebase.google.com/docs/app-c=
heck/android/debug-provider" target=3D"_blank">configure the debug provider=
 yourself</a> or you can <a href=3D"https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-log=
ic/app-check#unenforce-app-check" target=3D"_blank">temporarily un-enforce =
App Check for AI Logic</a>.</p>
</aside>


