         =20
         =20
         =20
          <p>Now that you've implemented Firebase PNV, it's time to run the=
 app.</p>
<ol type=3D"1">
<li>In Android Studio, click <strong>Run</strong> to launch the app in the =
Android emulator or on a physical device.</li>
<li>Once the app launches, you should see a screen that looks like this: <b=
r><img alt=3D"Firebase PNV app running" src=3D"https://firebase.google.com/=
static/codelabs/firebase-pnv-android/img/fpnv_android_1.png"></li>
<li>Click <strong>Start call</strong>, and introduce yourself. <br><img alt=
=3D"Firebase PNV app running" src=3D"https://firebase.google.com/static/cod=
elabs/firebase-pnv-android/img/fpnv_android_2.png"></li>
<li>The AI voice agent should prompt you for reservation details. Once you =
provide details, it should prompt you to look at your screen to verify your=
 phone number: <br><img alt=3D"Firebase PNV app running" src=3D"https://fir=
ebase.google.com/static/codelabs/firebase-pnv-android/img/fpnv_android_3.pn=
g"></li>
<li>Once that's done, you'll see a verification complete screen: <br><img a=
lt=3D"Firebase PNV app running" style=3D"width: 280.00px" src=3D"https://fi=
rebase.google.com/static/codelabs/firebase-pnv-android/img/fpnv_android_4.p=
ng"></li>
<li>Click <strong>End session</strong> to terminate the call.</li>
</ol>


