e-pnv-android#4">5. (Optional) Upgrade to production mode</a></h2>
         =20
         =20
         =20
          <h2 is-upgraded=3D"" id=3D"upgrade-your-firebase-pricing-plan" da=
ta-text=3D"Upgrade your Firebase pricing plan" tabindex=3D"-1">Upgrade your=
 Firebase pricing plan</h2>
<p>To use Firebase PNV in <strong>production mode</strong>, your Firebase p=
roject needs to be on the <a href=3D"https://firebase.google.com/docs/proje=
cts/billing/firebase-pricing-plans#blaze-pricing-plan" target=3D"_blank">pa=
y-as-you go (Blaze) pricing plan</a>, which means it's linked to a <a href=
=3D"https://firebase.google.com/docs/projects/billing/firebase-pricing-plan=
s#cloud-billing-accounts" target=3D"_blank">Cloud Billing account</a>.</p>
<ul>
<li>A Cloud Billing account requires a payment method, like a credit card.<=
/li>
<li>During special promotions or if you're doing this codelab as part of an=
 event, there may be Google Cloud credits available.</li>
<li>If you're new to Firebase and Google Cloud, check if you're eligible fo=
r a <a href=3D"https://firebase.google.com/support/faq#pricing-free-trial" =
target=3D"_blank">$300 credit and a Free Trial Cloud Billing account</a>.</=
li>
</ul>
<p>To upgrade your project to the Blaze plan, follow these steps:</p>
<ol type=3D"1">
<li>In the Firebase console, select to <a href=3D"https://console.firebase.=
google.com/project/_/overview?purchaseBillingPlan=3Dmetered" target=3D"_bla=
nk">upgrade your plan</a>.</li>
<li>Select the Blaze plan. Follow the on-screen instructions to link a Clou=
d Billing account to your project.<br><ul>
<li>If you're using Google Cloud credits for this codelab, the billing acco=
unt is likely called <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">Google Cloud Platfo=
rm Trial Billing Account</code> or <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">My Bi=
lling Account</code>.</li>
<li>If you needed to create a Cloud Billing account as part of this upgrade=
, you might need to navigate back to the upgrade flow in the Firebase conso=
le to complete the upgrade.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<h2 is-upgraded=3D"" id=3D"enable-firebase-pnv-production-mode" data-text=
=3D"Enable Firebase PNV production mode" tabindex=3D"-1">Enable Firebase PN=
V production mode</h2>
<ol type=3D"1">
<li>Add your app's SHA-256 fingerprint:<ol type=3D"1">
<li>In the Firebase console, go to the <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <a hr=
ef=3D"https://console.firebase.google.com/project/_/settings/general" targe=
t=3D"_blank"><strong>General</strong> page</a>.</li>
<li>Scroll down to the <strong>Your apps</strong> card, and find your Andro=
id app.</li>
<li>Into the <strong>SHA certificate fingerprints</strong> field, add your =
SHA-256 fingerprint. Refer to <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/andr=
oid/guides/client-auth" target=3D"_blank">Authenticating Your Client</a> fo=
r details on how to get your app's SHA-256 fingerprint.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Return to <strong>Security</strong> &gt; <a href=3D"https://console.fir=
ebase.google.com/project/_/phoneverification" target=3D"_blank"><strong>Pho=
ne Verification</strong></a>.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Set up production</strong>. You will see a list of the ap=
ps in your project that will be enabled for production, and have the opport=
unity to add additional apps.</li>
<li>Submit your app for <a href=3D"https://support.google.com/cloud/answer/=
13464321?sjid=3D16326092754406046967-NC" target=3D"_blank">OAuth brand veri=
fication</a> and a privacy policy review. Google Cloud will verify that you=
 are clearly and accurately identifying your app and its privacy policy.<br=
>To begin the review, click <strong>Proceed in Google Cloud</strong>. This =
process can sometimes take 24 hours or more.</li>
<li>While you're waiting for brand verification, review the Firebase PNV se=
rvice specific terms, which are linked to in the console.</li>
<li>After your app has passed brand verification, check the box to acknowle=
dge the service specific terms, and then click <strong>Enable</strong>.</li=
>
</ol>
<p>Firebase PNV is now active in production mode.</p>
<h2 is-upgraded=3D"" id=3D"remove-test-code" data-text=3D"Remove test code"=
 tabindex=3D"-1">Remove test code</h2>
<p>In your Android project, delete the line <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"l=
tr">fpnv.enableTestSession(...)</code>.</p>
<h2 is-upgraded=3D"" id=3D"migrate-firebase-ai-logic-to-use-vertex-ai" data=
-text=3D"Migrate Firebase AI Logic to use Vertex AI" tabindex=3D"-1">Migrat=
e Firebase AI Logic to use Vertex AI</h2>
<p>If you're using credits in your billing account, you won't be able to us=
e them with the Gemini Developer API. But you can use them with the Vertex =
AI Gemini API.</p>
<ol type=3D"1">
<li>In the Firebase console, go to <strong>AI Services</strong> &gt; <a hre=
f=3D"https://console.firebase.google.com/project/_/ailogic/" target=3D"_bla=
nk"><strong>AI Logic</strong></a>.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Under <em>Vertex AI Gemini API</em>, click <strong>Enable</strong>.</li=
>
<li>In your Android project, change the Firebase AI Logic initialization to=
 use the Vertex AI backend instead of Google AI:<div></div><devsite-code da=
ta-copy-event-label=3D""><pre class=3D"" translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr" is-up=
graded=3D"" syntax=3D"Text only" syntax-guessed=3D""><code language=3D"lang=
uage-kotlin" class=3D"language-kotlin" translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr"><span c=
lass=3D"pln">val model </span><span class=3D"pun">=3D</span><span class=3D"=
pln"> </span><span class=3D"typ">Firebase</span><span class=3D"pun">.</span=
><span class=3D"pln">ai</span><span class=3D"pun">(</span><span class=3D"pl=
n"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; backend </span><span class=3D"pun">=3D</span><span cla=
ss=3D"pln"> </span><span class=3D"typ">GenerativeBackend</span><span class=
=3D"pun">.</span><span class=3D"pln">vertexAI</span><span class=3D"pun">(</=
span><span class=3D"pln">location </span><span class=3D"pun">=3D</span><spa=
n class=3D"pln"> </span><span class=3D"str">"us-central1"</span><span class=
=3D"pun">)</span><span class=3D"pln"><br></span><span class=3D"pun">).</spa=
n><span class=3D"pln">liveModel</span><span class=3D"pun">(</span><span cla=
ss=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; modelName </span><span class=3D"pun">=3D</span=
><span class=3D"pln"> </span><span class=3D"str">"gemini-live-2.5-flash-nat=
ive-audio"</span><span class=3D"pun">,</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp;=
 &nbsp; </span><span class=3D"com">// ... other configuration</span><span c=
lass=3D"pln"><br></span><span class=3D"pun">)</span><span class=3D"pln"><br=
></span></code></pre></devsite-code>
</li>
</ol>


